nd get the edge on the competition with power-ups, fireball pitches, super strength, and Pablo Sanchez!\nPlay pick-up games, practice batting, and compete in single games or a whole season with simple, intuitive controls that anyone can master!\nGame Modes:\nRandom Pick-up: A quick way to jump right in! The computer chooses a random team for you and itself, and the game starts immediately.\nSingle Game: You take turns with the computer to choose players from a random pool of characters.\nSeason: You create a team and manage it through a 14 game series. The opposing teams are computer generated. At the end of the season the best two teams advance to the BBL playoffs (best of 3). The winner advances to the championship series which consists of the Super Entire Nation Tournament (best of 3) and then the Ultra Grand Championship of the Universe Series (best of 5)!\nBatting Practice: Choose a batter and face Mr. Clanky for some batting practice. This is where you’ll learn just when to click to make your chosen batter hit that ball!\nT-ball - Select T-ball mode for more accessible game play. Simply click to hit, run, and field!\n \nBACKYARD BASEBALL RULES\nThe rules for Backyard Baseball are a hybrid of Pro and Little League rules:\nNo leading off\nNo Injuries\nBunting is allowed\nTagging up is allowed\nStealing is allowed\n \nAt our core, we are fans first–not just of video games but of the Backyard Sports franchise. Fans have asked for accessible and legal ways to play their original Backyard titles for years, and we are excited to deliver. Without having access to the source code, there are hard limitations on the experience we can create. Backyard Baseball '97 runs buttery smooth for iOS devices, looks better than ever, and creates a new installation for digital preservation within the Backyard Sports catalog that allows the next generation of fans to fall in love with the title that started it all.", "bundleId": "com.megacatstudios.backyardbaseball", "userRatingCount": 3}]}